 receiving**, use **Implementation plan tasks** for accepted custom work or select the original workorder edition for work tied to it. Record the actual technical or customer observation and its source reference.\n5. In **Export and reopen**, choose **Open complete case handoff**. The original complete-delivery desk saves the case and retains the export and receiving operations for its full history, source bundles and attachments.\n\nLater quotation revisions continue through the same review and acceptance workflow. The receiving case keeps the original agreement and accepted changes alongside the delivered work.\n\n## Tariff quotation and editable handover\n\nOpen **Applications → Merchant pricing and scenario planning → Tariff planning** to retain the original schedule, compare exact quantities and complete its selected scenario and pricing requests. In **Applications → Merchant support → Commercial quotations**, choose the saved customer case and open **Tariff sources**.\n\nCapture the completed original selection with its full pricing backup, inspect the retained source and attach it through the original case writer. The quote keeps its selected quantity, saved uniform rate, original tier total and rounding. A changed monthly quantity displays the original tariff calculation alongside the saved-rate charge.\n\nContinue the accepted quotation into implementation and receiving. The complete case package carries the original tariff source and pricing backup with its quote editions, customer responses and delivery history. In the receiving case, restore the original pricing workspace, receive the selected portfolio and reopen both saved native outcomes.\n\nThe maintained commands are `starforge merchant-tariffs`, `starforge merchant-commercial tariffs` and the original `merchant-mcp pricing` and Support tools. The linked tariff guide provides the complete capture, three-request attachment, download, export and restoration inputs.\n\n## Recorded usage through the next customer quotation\n\nUse the original Pricing console's **Performance** page to compare a completed tariff selection with a saved usage source. The observed period, exact count basis, saved uniform quote and original tariff curve remain explicit. Save the review and export its complete original source.\n\nIn **Merchant support → Commercial quotations → Usage and revisions**, receive that full source against the measured original quote. Select the retained review, enter an explicit monthly request volume and choose the existing or a newer received native tariff for the same route. Prepare the ordinary quote draft, then complete its original review, publication, customer-response and accepted-work flow.\n\nThe full customer case carries the performance source as an original material. Its receiving case can inspect and export that source immediately. Complete native continuation uses an original Pricing workspace backup captured after the review and proposal operations, plus the full tariff portfolio. Restore that backup, receive the portfolio through its original owner and reopen Performance to recover the same saved proposal and selection requests.\n\nThe package includes `starforge merchant-performance`, `starforge merchant-commercial performance`, the typed `./merchant/performance-client` and `./merchant/commercial-performance-client` exports, and the original Pricing and Support MCP methods. Both linked performance guides describe the exact inputs, source identities, native request UUIDs, downloads and continuation.\n\n## Accepted quotations through billing and the service calendar\n\nSelect the published quotation in the saved customer case and download its complete quotation JSON and matching accepted response. Open **Applications → Merchant receivables** or **Applications → Service agreements and billing** with the merchant's original initialized accounting directory and customer.\n\nThe invoice import retains the selected tariff and measured-usage source alongside the accepted revised amount. Its view separates the observed period and quantity from the explicitly quoted monthly volume and uniform rate. Review the source, billing scope, dates and resulting draft, then issue it through the original Receivables writer.\n\nFor ongoing work, create the service agreement from that same accepted source. Review its original monthly boundaries, billing periods and current quotation edition. Preparing a period creates the original invoice draft; later editions, renewals and cancellation preserve the previous calendar and bills. The same combined server exposes customer records, receivables and the service calendar under one accounting lease.\n\nThe package includes the original payment plans, Stellar collection, paid credits, refunds and customer statement closing. Its typed clients and merchant tools continue to use the original Accounting and service-agreement controllers.\n\n- [Complete invoicing, payment and refund workflow](source/products/merchant-receivables/README.md)\n- [Accepted agreements and recurring billing](source/products/merchant-service-agreements/README.md)\n- [Payment plans and dated collections](source/products/merchant-payment-plans/README.md)\n- [Complete financial operation](source/products/merchant-workspace/FINANCIAL_OPERATIONS.md)\n\n## Commands\n\nThe installed `starforge` command includes `receivables`, `service-agreements`, `payment-plans`, `customer-closing`, `merchant-accounting-receivables`, `merchant-accounting-pricing`, `merchant-accounting-recovery`, `support-console`, `support-watch`, `merchant-implementation`, `merchant-services`, `merchant-commercial`, `merchant-tariffs`, `merchant-performance`, `merchant-support-agent`, `merchant-service-adjustments`, `merchant-service-adjustment-receiving`, `merchant-accounting-adjustments`, `buyer-expenses`, the original merchant MCP launchers, and the maintained runtime installation and transfer commands.\n\nRead the setup command's original options:\n\n```sh\nstarforge merchant-support-agent --help\n```\n\nThe setup command creates the original merchant host for an existing Support connection and case collection. Its original release initialization and immutable configuration publication resume in the same selected output.\n\n## Continue customer work\n\nReceive the whole case package through **Complete delivery**, then open the receiving case named by the original completion. Keep that case directory and native source directory together through reopening. The package retains the complete captured sender history and every original native source archive.\n"
